<BaseLayout
  title="About SportsRulesDesk"
  description="SportsRulesDesk explains NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL and Fantasy sports rules in plain English, sourced from official league rulebooks."
  current="about"
>
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <h1>About SportsRulesDesk</h1>
    <p>
      SportsRulesDesk is a reference site focused on one thing: explaining how sports rules
      actually work. No live scores, no daily news cycle, just clear breakdowns of rules,
      penalties, and scoring systems across NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, NCAA, and Fantasy sports.
    </p>
    <h2>Why we exist</h2>
    <p>
      Official rulebooks are long, dense, and full of legal language. Sports commentary
      often assumes you already know the rule being discussed. SportsRulesDesk sits between
      the two: accurate enough to trust, simple enough to actually read.
    </p>
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>
      Fans who want to understand a rule after seeing it applied in a game, fantasy players
      making roster decisions, and anyone tired of vague explanations from commentators.
    </p>
    <h2>A part of fdaytalk.com</h2>
    <p>
      SportsRulesDesk is operated as a property of fdaytalk.com, a technology and gaming
      publication. This site follows the same editorial standard: sourced, accurate, and
      written to be genuinely useful rather than padded for length.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
